The layout comparison confirmed why the H-major pack exists: letting PyTorch handle a non-contiguous channel-last contraction was far slower. I’m checking the layer norm path next; the custom kernel is simple, but PyTorch’s native kernel may be faster for the wider `C=384/768` correctness cases.
